- Tab (on body)
- Enter (on #open) -> opens modal
- Space (on #weekly) -> should toggle checkbox but modal closes

The issue is that the Space key on a checkbox triggers a click event (since checkboxes respond to Space). That click event bubbles up to the overlay (which has data-micromodal-close). The onClick handler sees that the event.target.closest(`[${this.config.closeTrigger}]`) is the overlay (because the overlay has the close trigger attribute). The previous fix tried to check if the closeElement is the modal (overlay) and event.target is not the modal, then return. But note: the modal in the code is the outer modal element (the one with id="prefs-modal"), not the overlay. The overlay is a child of the modal. The closeTrigger is on the overlay (data-micromodal-close). So the closest element with the closeTrigger is the overlay. The condition in the previous fix was:

if (closeElement === this.modal && event.target !== this.modal) { return }

But this.modal is the outer modal (id="prefs-modal"), not the overlay. So closeElement (the overlay) is not equal to this.modal. Therefore the condition fails and the modal closes.

We need to adjust the condition to check if the closeElement is the overlay (or more generally, if the click originated from inside the modal container and not on the overlay background). The overlay is the element with the closeTrigger that is the background. The modal container is inside the overlay. We want to allow clicks on the modal container (including the checkbox) to not close the modal, but clicks on the overlay background (the dark area) to close.

